cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "differential-homing: differential abundance analysis of phage display peptide counts"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pleiko
    given-names: Karlis
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1073-197X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KarlisPleiko/differential-homing"
url: "https://github.com/KarlisPleiko/differential-homing"
abstract: >-
  differential-homing identifies peptides that are differentially abundant in a target tissue relative
  to a control tissue in phage display biopanning experiments. Peptide count tables from
  sequenced samples are joined on peptide sequence, restricted to a reference peptide list, and
  tested with edgeR's negative-binomial framework using TMM normalisation and a
  quasi-likelihood F-test, falling back to an assumed dispersion where a group lacks
  replicates. Abundance relative to the injected input library is summarised separately with
  propagated uncertainty. Outputs comprise the differential abundance table, ratio statistics,
  volcano and ranked-ratio figures, and per-file diagnostics. Implemented as a local Shiny
  application so that sequencing data never leave the user's machine.
keywords:
  - phage display
  - biopanning
  - differential abundance
  - edgeR
  - peptide library
  - in vivo homing
  - Shiny
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: "phader: peptide insert counting for T7 phage display sequencing data"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pleiko
        given-names: Karlis
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1073-197X"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/KarlisPleiko/phader"
    notes: "Produces the peptide count tables differential-homing consumes."
